    "key": "q1",
    "subject": "Your kit is ordered. Start tonight.",
    "html": "<!doctype html><html lang=\"en\"><head><meta charset=\"utf-8\"><meta name=\"viewport\" content=\"width=device-width,initial-scale=1\"><meta name=\"color-scheme\" content=\"light\"><title>Child Phenoms</title></head>\n<body style=\"margin:0;padding:0;background:#f6f7fb;color:#121826;font-family:-apple-system,BlinkMacSystemFont,'Segoe UI',Roboto,Helvetica,Arial,sans-serif\">\n<div style=\"display:none;max-height:0;overflow:hidden;opacity:0\">The 3-Night Quick-Start is inside.</div>\n<table role=\"presentation\" width=\"100%\" cellspacing=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" style=\"background:#f6f7fb\"><tr><td align=\"center\" style=\"padding:24px 12px\">\n<table role=\"presentation\" width=\"100%\" cellspacing=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" style=\"max-width:560px;background:#ffffff;border-radius:16px\"><tr><td style=\"padding:28px 26px 24px\">\n<p style=\"margin:0 0 22px;font-weight:800;font-size:18px;color:#121826\">Child <span style=\"color:#2457f5\">Phenoms</span></p>\n<p style=\"margin:0 0 18px;font-size:17px;line-height:1.55\">Hi {{first_name}},</p>\n<p style=\"margin:0 0 18px;font-size:17px;line-height:1.55\">Thank you. Your kit is ordered.</p>\n<p style=\"margin:0 0 18px;font-size:17px;line-height:1.55\">The card receipt says Enamelogic. That is our parent company. Same team, same people.</p>\n<p style=\"margin:0 0 18px;font-size:17px;line-height:1.55\">The box ships within 2 business days with tracking. Most kits arrive in 9 to 15 days. You do not have to wait for it. Your first three nights are at the bottom of this email. They work on the screen abacus in your parent account tonight.</p>\n<p style=\"margin:0 0 18px;font-size:17px;line-height:1.55\">{{if_bump}}Your Playbook and the audiobook are waiting too. Sign in and look under &quot;What you own.&quot;{{end_if}}</p>\n<p style=\"margin:0 0 18px;font-size:17px;line-height:1.55\">First, I want you to see something.</p>\n<p style=\"margin:0 0 18px;font-size:17px;line-height:1.55\">About a million kids in Japan learn this every year. On a stage, one child added fifteen 3-digit numbers in 1.61 seconds. A world record.</p>\n<p style=\"margin:0 0 18px;font-size:17px;line-height:1.55\">Most parents watch that and think: that kid is a genius.</p>\n<p style=\"margin:0 0 18px;font-size:17px;line-height:1.55\">I thought so too. Then I learned the secret.</p>\n<p style=\"margin:0 0 18px;font-size:17px;line-height:1.55\">That child is not doing math. The child is looking at a picture. Beads, in the mind. The hands learned the beads first. Then the eyes. Then the picture moved inside the head.</p>\n<p style=\"margin:0 0 18px;font-size:17px;line-height:1.55\">That is the whole trick. And any child can build the picture.</p>\n<p style=\"margin:0 0 18px;font-size:17px;line-height:1.55\">I know, because I built it late. I was the kid teachers gave up on. C's in math. ADHD. Then I needed a big test score to play college sports. So I did fifteen minutes a day with the beads. Around week three, something clicked. Numbers stopped being things to memorize. They became things I could move. I got a perfect ACT and a full ride.</p>\n<p style=\"margin:0 0 18px;font-size:17px;line-height:1.55\">Your child gets to start at seven, not seventeen.</p>\n<p style=\"margin:0 0 18px;font-size:17px;line-height:1.55\">Here is why it works. School uses half the brain. Words and memory. The beads wake up the other half. Pictures and hands. Your child sees the number, moves it, and says it. All of the brain at once. I call it whole brain. That is my word, not a lab word. But the brain scans back it up. Abacus kids do sums with the parts of the brain that handle pictures and hand moves.</p>\n<p style=\"margin:0 0 18px;font-size:17px;line-height:1.55\">Here is why it lasts. In a three-year study, normal kids who trained on the abacus beat kids who got extra math class. Another study followed 144 children. Five years later, the abacus kids still did better on memory tests for shapes and space. That is not a trick for one test. That is a brain that works differently, for life.</p>\n<p style=\"margin:0 0 18px;font-size:17px;line-height:1.55\">Your part is small. Fifteen minutes a night, beside your child. You do not teach. The trainer picks every problem. You praise the move, not the answer.</p>\n<p style=\"margin:0 0 18px;font-size:17px;line-height:1.55\">Tomorrow I will send you the plan: the three steps every abacus child walks, and the week where most families quit.</p>\n<p style=\"margin:0 0 18px;font-size:17px;line-height:1.55\">Hunter</p>\n<hr style=\"border:0;border-top:2px solid #e6e8ef;margin:26px 0\">\n<h2 style=\"margin:28px 0 14px;font-size:22px;line-height:1.25;color:#121826\">Your 3-Night Quick-Start</h2>\n<p style=\"margin:0 0 18px;font-size:17px;line-height:1.55\">Start tonight on the screen abacus: <a href=\"https://childphenoms.com/#/stage/1\" style=\"color:#2457f5;text-decoration:underline\">childphenoms.com/#/stage/1</a>. Sign in with the email you ordered with. When the box lands, do the same three nights again with the real beads.</p>\n<p style=\"margin:0 0 18px;font-size:17px;line-height:1.55\"><b>Every night:</b> 15 minutes. Sit beside, not across. Say each move out loud. Praise the move, not the answer. Stop while it is still fun.</p>\n<p style=\"margin:0 0 18px;font-size:17px;line-height:1.55\"><b>Night 1 · See it, move it, say it</b><br>Push all the beads away from the beam. Thumb pushes beads up. Pointer finger pushes them down. Bottom beads are 1. The top bead is 5. A bead counts when it touches the beam. Set 1 to 9 out loud. Stuck? Ask, &quot;Free beads, or friend?&quot; Then wait.<br>Why tonight matters: the hands learn the beads. That is the first half of the picture.</p>\n<p style=\"margin:0 0 18px;font-size:17px;line-height:1.55\"><b>Night 2 · Bigger numbers</b><br>Left rod is tens. Right rod is ones. Set 23, 47 and 85. Read each one back. Then cover the abacus and ask, &quot;What did 47 look like?&quot;<br>Why tonight matters: the picture starts to move inside.</p>\n<p style=\"margin:0 0 18px;font-size:17px;line-height:1.55\"><b>Night 3 · The first friend move</b><br>Set 4. Add 1. No free bead! Bring the 5 down and send 4 away. Plus 1 is plus 5, take away 4. Not yet? That is fine. Stage 2 teaches it.<br>Why tonight matters: this is where numbers stop being memorized and start being moved.</p>\n<p style=\"margin:0 0 18px;font-size:17px;line-height:1.55\"><b>Night 4:</b> Lesson 1 is in your parent account: <a href=\"https://childphenoms.com/#/stage/1/lesson/hold\" style=\"color:#2457f5;text-decoration:underline\">childphenoms.com/#/stage/1/lesson/hold</a>. Questions? Reply to this email.</p>\n<p style=\"margin:0 0 18px;font-size:17px;line-height:1.55\">P.S. Tonight, Night 1. Ten minutes is enough: <a href=\"https://childphenoms.com/#/stage/1\" style=\"color:#2457f5;text-decoration:underline\">childphenoms.com/#/stage/1</a></p>\n<div style=\"margin-top:34px;padding-top:16px;border-top:1px solid #e6e8ef;font-size:12px;line-height:1.5;color:#6b7280\"><p style=\"margin:0 0 6px\">Child Phenoms, a DBA of Enamelogic LLC · 1309 Coffeen Avenue STE 1200, Sheridan, WY 82801 · hello@childphenoms.com</p><p style=\"margin:0 0 6px\">You get this because you ordered a kit or started an order at childphenoms.com. Unsubscribe: {{unsubscribe}}</p><p style=\"margin:0 0 6px\">Research cited describes group averages in published trials. Your child's progress depends on practice.</p><p style=\"margin:0 0 6px\">Instructor earnings are not promised. What you charge is up to you.</p></div>\n</td></tr></table>\n</td></tr></table>\n</body></html>",
